      url: "/portraits/henry-david-thoreau-maxham-1856.jpg",
      source: "Ninth-plate daguerreotype of Henry David Thoreau by Benjamin D. Maxham (1821-1899), made at his studio in Worcester, Massachusetts, in June 1856, National Portrait Gallery, Smithsonian Institution, Washington (object NPG.72.119, gift of an anonymous donor). A documented sitting during the sitter's lifetime. The file is a plain crop of the plate from the museum's own 3345 x 4000 pixel scan of the cased object (the case and mat are cut away), downscaled to 871 x 1200 with no upscaling and no retouching.",
