      url: "/portraits/hertha-ayrton-unknown-1899.jpg",
      source: "Studio photograph of Hertha Ayrton, reproduced as a small printed halftone in the 'Who's Who' album of the International Congress of Women, London, June 1899 (caption 'Mrs Ayrton'); photographer not named. The scan is from the Charlotte Perkins Gilman Papers, Schlesinger Library, Radcliffe Institute, Harvard University (Collection 177, folder 6), page about 2682 x 1828 pixels, and the Wikimedia Commons copy is a circular-portrait crop of that page, 383 x 387 pixels. The same pose, hair and brooch appear in a Library of Congress Bain News Service photograph of Hertha Ayrton, which is how the identification was checked. A printed publication of 1899 is in the public domain in the United States by age (published before 1931) and, with no named photographer, in the United Kingdom. The file is used at its original 383 x 387 size, with no resizing or upscaling.",
      license: "Public domain (published in 1899)",
