      // [src_hmann_britannica, src_hmann_uxl, src_hmann_mhs | 1838-1853 | reference entries, archival timeline] He founded and edited the Common School Journal (1838), toured and organised county meetings across the state, worked with a philanthropist's matching gift toward normal schools, and later accepted the founding presidency of Antioch. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): reviewed as a top-risk row; lowered from 72 / 0.52 to 68 / 0.48 because the normal-school credit is shared in the sources with other reformers and the philanthropist, and the Encyclopedia of Education places him within a wider movement.
