      // [src_hmann_britannica, src_hmann_uxl | 1837-1848 | reference entries] Britannica summarises his reports as six connected propositions (universal education, public control and payment, mixed schools, nonsectarian moral content, humane method, trained professional teachers), and the Gale biography credits him with guidelines on teacher standards, a defined school year and curriculum standards. These are later summaries of a coherent design rather than evidence of how he reasoned, so the confidence is low.
