      source: "Portrait of Nikolai Ivanovich Lobachevsky, oil on canvas, by Lev Dmitrievich Kryukov (1783-1843), the painter employed at Kazan University, dated to the first half of the nineteenth century and in other lists to the 1830s or 1839, so painted in the sitter's lifetime by a painter who died in 1843. Because the painter died in 1843 the painting is in the public domain by age everywhere, and a faithful photograph of a flat painting adds no new copyright. The file is the unaltered 600 x 800 pixel image from Wikimedia Commons, whose page cites a Tatarstan museums-portal page (tatar.museum.ru, section 'univer') as its source; that page could not be opened, so the present owner of the canvas and any museum notice were not checked. No cropping, no resizing and no upscaling.",
