      url: "/portraits/nikolay-przhevalsky-engraving-1887.jpg",
      source: "Wood engraving of Nicholas Prejevalski published as the illustration to 'Sketch of Nicholas Prejevalski', Popular Science Monthly, volume 30 (January 1887), page 304 (plate D304), engraver not identified (a signature at lower left is illegible). Hosted on Wikimedia Commons as 'PSM V30 D304 Nicholas Prejevalsky.jpg' from the Internet Archive scan of the volume; I opened the Wikisource article that carries it. Rights basis: first published in the United States in 1887, so in the public domain in the United States by publication date regardless of the engraver; no institutional notice conflicts (the periodical's own pages are the source and carry no restriction). The Commons file page gives only a generic old-work tag, so the basis rests on the documented 1887 publication. Original scan 1759 x 2335 pixels, downscaled with no cropping to 904 x 1200; never upscaled. An engraving is a depiction made in his lifetime from an unstated source, not a documented sitting, so it is classed as a historical depiction like other engravings in this roster.",
